{
  "summary": "The Lean theorem is a one-step, coefficient-level statement about a single harmonic, under many structural hypotheses. A corrected linear wave is built from a source in WaveClass α. The theorem proves three things: the 'good' part lies in WaveClass (α + 1/2 − 3κ); an excluded-slot error lies in UnweightedClass for every real N; and an exact pointwise identity holds, residual + source·carrier = (good + error)·carrier. Paper Proposition 9.3 is a statement about the full iterated construction (u^[j], p^[j]), and the pairing may be loose. It covers the physical decomposition R = G + F, harmonic support structure, the physical flat bound |F|_m ≤ C q^N, and exact mean equations. Lean captures at most a single-step analogue of the 'G + F with F flat' part. Key caveats: (iii) and most of (i) are not formalized, and several hypotheses (ExactConditions on the corrected coefficients, hsolve, a band-independent radius) assume properties of the construction.",
  "glossary": [
    {"decl": "BandBound", "line": 4, "plain": "a_n is O(ε_n^β · slow_n^p) uniformly in the band n, for some constant C ≥ 0 and some p ∈ ℕ.", "standard_concept": "band-uniform weighted bound", "matches_standard": "yes", "note": "Used in hK with a_n = 1/frequency_n. If frequency_n = 0, the junk value 1/0 = 0 makes the bound trivial at that n."},
    {"decl": "BandScaleControl", "line": 12, "plain": "Data with ε_n = Q_n^power for a real exponent, and slow_n ≤ C(1+S_n)^deg with C ≥ 1.", "standard_concept": "scale identity ε = Q^{power} with polynomial slow-scale control", "matches_standard": "unclear", "note": "Paper scale conventions are not in the excerpt."},
    {"decl": "D", "line": 26, "plain": "The shown definition is D(h) = 1/2 − h, a real function.", "standard_concept": "presumably the spatial domain type", "matches_standard": "unclear", "note": "The theorem uses D as a type (StripData D, D → ℝ), so this extracted definition cannot be the one in scope. The actual D is not visible."},
    {"decl": "ExactConditions", "line": 31, "plain": "On s.domain: the phases are smooth; the radius is nonzero and has unit radial derivative; the base, amplitude and pressure are annihilated by the angular field; and each phase has constant angular derivative.", "standard_concept": "local geometric/angular conditions for the exact residual identity", "matches_standard": "unclear", "note": "Imposed on the corrected coefficients (an output of the construction)."},
    {"decl": "FlatEdges", "line": 47, "plain": "Two positive decay rates, a width, and a position map into (0, width) on the domain, with δ given by the radial primitive formula and ζ bounded by the two-sided exponential-flat profile.", "standard_concept": "two-sided exponentially flat edge cutoff", "matches_standard": "unclear", "note": "WeightedRadialPrimitive.delta and zeta are not shown."},
    {"decl": "ComplexVector", "line": 22, "plain": "Alias of HarmonicCalculus.ComplexVector, presumably ℂ^3.", "standard_concept": "C^3-valued coefficients", "matches_standard": "unclear", "note": "Definition not shown."}
  ],
  "lean_claims": [
    {"theorem": "constructed_linear_wave_with_flat_error", "line": 63, "plain": "Assume the following hypotheses:\n- InputBounds s P α κ d a, and κ ≤ 1/2.\n- A slot family g with linear(fastScale·fast) = 1/length.\n- Flat edges and band-scale control data.\n- source ∈ WaveClass s P α.\n- A Gaussian bound P_n(x) ≤ exp(−c(coord_n(x) − 1/2)^2 · length_n) with c > 0.\n- A band-independent radius R.\n- Polynomial jet bounds on the normal, and 0 < b ≤ |normal| ≤ M on the domain.\n- 1/frequency_n bounded by ε_n^{1/2} times a slow polynomial.\n- principal = −source on the domain.\n- ExactConditions for the corrected coefficients.\nThen three conclusions hold:\n(1) constructedGood ∈ WaveClass s P (α + 1/2 − 3κ);\n(2) the excluded-slot error lies in UnweightedClass s N for every real N;\n(3) for all n and x in the domain, harmonicResidual(corrected)_n(x) + source_n(x)·carrier = (constructedGood_n(x) + error_n(x))·carrier."}
  ],
  "paper_claims": [
    {"ref": "Proposition 9.3", "plain": "After any finite sequence of the construction steps, with pressure reconstructed, the physical residual decomposes as R(u^[j], p^[j]) = G^[j] + F^[j]. (i) The nonzero harmonics of G* are a finite band-independent set of harmonics, with supported smooth coefficients in W_α and mean in M_µ. (ii) |F^[j]|_m ≤ C_{j,m,N} q^N for all m and N, uniformly over bands, labels and points. (iii) Exact mean equations (9.6) hold."}
  ],
  "coverage": [
    {"paper_ref": "Proposition 9.3 (overall, iterated construction)", "lean_theorem": "constructed_linear_wave_with_flat_error", "relation": "lean_weaker", "why": "Lean treats one wave-construction step for one harmonic coefficient, not the finite iterated sequence with pressure reconstruction."},
    {"paper_ref": "Proposition 9.3 (i) coefficient class", "lean_theorem": "constructed_linear_wave_with_flat_error", "relation": "lean_weaker", "why": "Only the W-class membership of the good coefficient is formalized, with an explicit exponent α + 1/2 − 3κ. The finite harmonic set H_j, supports and smooth zero extension are not formalized."},
    {"paper_ref": "Proposition 9.3 (ii) flat remainder", "lean_theorem": "constructed_linear_wave_with_flat_error", "relation": "lean_weaker", "why": "Lean gives UnweightedClass for all N at coefficient level. Whether this equals the physical |F|_m ≤ C q^N uniform bound cannot be checked, because UnweightedClass is not shown."},
    {"paper_ref": "Proposition 9.3 (iii) mean equations", "lean_theorem": null, "relation": "not_formalized", "why": "No mean-equation statement appears."}
  ],
